MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset="utf-8"
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Hands down, I would say S-X2 is the best choice of the item fit measures available. But don't take my word for it, I'd recommend checking out the original sources since they talk about other item fit measures and compare them in good depth via simulation work. Specifically,

Orlando, M. & Thissen, D. (2000). Likelihood-based item fit indices for dichotomous item response theory models. Applied Psychological Measurement, 24, 50-64.

As well as a later one by the same authors in APM about more severe model violations. Cheers.

Phil

