Hi Irshad,

There's a lot of questions here that could probably be answered better by looking over texts on computerized adaptive testing, but I'll try and respond to them in a concise manner.

On Fri, Sep 12, 2014 at 3:04 AM, Irshad Mujawar <irshadmuj...@gmail.com> wrote:

> Hello Phil,
>
> For calibration purpose,  I observed that you need minimum 3 items to go to the calibration ( at least for Rasch model)
>
> I was experimenting with the LSAT7 data, which has 5 items in it. I calibrated first 3 items separately using Rasch 1 factor model.
>

> > raschfit=mirt(data[,1:3], 1, 'Rasch')
> Iteration: 83, Log-Lik: -1594.718, Max-Change: 0.00010
> > coef(raschfit)

